## 2. Measurable KPIs and Success Metrics

Success is measured through a **balanced scorecard** combining traditional usability metrics, AI-specific performance signals, and craft quality indicators. The AI designer is evaluated on **output and impact, not effort**.

### 2.1 Quantitative Metrics

| Metric | Definition | Target | Measurement Method |
|---|---|---|---|
| **System Usability Scale (SUS)** | Standardized 10-item questionnaire measuring perceived usability | >75 (Good) | Post-test questionnaires administered during user testing |
| **Task Completion Rate** | Percentage of users who complete core tasks without assistance | >90% for primary journeys | Analytics + moderated testing |
| **Time-on-Task** | Median time to complete successful task attempts | Reduction vs. baseline | Session replay analytics |
| **Error Rate** | Frequency of mis-clicks, wrong paths, and recovery actions | <5% per core flow | Clickstream analytics |
| **Design System Adoption Rate** | Percentage of production components linked to official ADS library | >85% | Automated audits (component tracking) |
| **Accessibility Compliance** | Adherence to WCAG 2.1 Level AA across all shipped surfaces | 100% | Automated + manual audits |
| **Design Debt Reduction Velocity** | Rate at which `design-debt` tagged issues are resolved | Sprint-over-sprint improvement | Jira backlog tracking |
| **Prototype-to-Implementation Fidelity** | Pixel-perfect and behavioral fidelity between design and production | >95% match score | VRT tools + manual spot-checks |
| **Design System "Days Behind"** | Time between component release and product adoption | <14 days | Component version tracking |

### 2.2 Qualitative Metrics

| Metric | Definition | Measurement Method |
|---|---|---|
| **Stakeholder Satisfaction** | PM and Engineering partner satisfaction with design collaboration | Quarterly feedback surveys (1–5 scale) |
| **Design Consistency** | Peer review scores assessing visual and interaction consistency | Weekly critique session scoring |
| **AI Value Expression** | User trust and perceived value of AI-mediated interactions | CSAT surveys + trust-specific Likert scales |
| **Design Decision Quality** | Ratio of design decisions that survive implementation without rework | Post-ship retrospective analysis |

### 2.3 AI-Specific Performance Metrics

| Metric | Definition | Target |
|---|---|---|
| **Rubric Compliance Score** | Score against AI Design Rubric (Trust, Error Handling, A11y) | >90% per artifact |
| **Time-to-Delegation** | How quickly the team trusts the AI for routine iterations | Decreasing over first 3 months |
| **Resolution Rate** | Effectiveness of AI-driven design suggestions accepted by team | >70% acceptance rate |
| **AI Maturity Labeling** | Categorization of work as Frontier, Emerging, or Scale | Majority at "Scale" within 6 months |
| **Autonomous Completion Rate** | Percentage of tasks completed without escalation | >80% for Tier 1 tasks |

